WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.970
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
With enough salmon

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.538
for the final cook,
I'm off to meet

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:09.542
a guy who's been innovative with
Iceland's geothermal energy.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:13.680
I'm told he has a very
unusual way of baking bread.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.051
Siggi.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:18.985
Hey.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.053
How are you, captain?

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.121
Very good.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:21.955
Good to see you, man.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:22.622
Good to see you.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.590
Oh, boy.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:24.224
Are you good?

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.258
Yeah, very good.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.659
That is a very firm handshake.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.027
Yeah, good grip.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:28.928
Good grip.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.163
What's going on here?

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.031
I want to show you
a real rye bread.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.433
Right, a rye bread?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.300
Yeah.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.236
I mean, my gran
makes rye bread.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.737
So what's your secret
about this one?

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:41.141
I can promise you she never
made rye bread like this.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.642
We got here I have
4 cups of rye.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.343
Yep.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.544
And 2 cups of flour--

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:45.178
Right

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.079
In the same bowl.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.414
How old is this recipe?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.149
Is it a recipe from the
family, traditions or--

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.084
Yeah, it is, late
1800s early 1900s.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.619
Yeah.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:53.453
Good.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.522
Yes, then you put on a glove.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.289
The glove?

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.224
Yeah, one glove.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.159
Little butter.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.059
You got a problem?

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.361
Bend over.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.529
Take a little butter.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.463
Yes.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.431
And you--

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.165
Gotcha.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:06.032
All of this and--

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:06.666
All of it?

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.700
Yep.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.202
And that's it?

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.503
We don't leave it to prove
for 10 minutes or anything?

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:10.904
No?

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.205
No.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.207
So where are we going
to bake this thing?

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.776
The ground is
boiling underneath us.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:17.944
Really?

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:20.880
It's a very active
hot spring area.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.950
Right here in this village
we have a huge hot spring,

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.385
and we used to heat
up the village.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.187
All from these
hot springs here?

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.723
The geothermal literally
takes care of all the heating?

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.091
Absolutely, Yeah.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.126
Wow, gotcha.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.027
Is that enough?

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:34.994
That's enough.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:35.929
All right.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.131
So where's the oven?

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.966
Right over there.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.234
We have to do a little work.

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.902
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
And by work, he

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.938
means digging my
own oven and burning

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.973
volcanic Earth with a shovel.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.842
And by we, he means me.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.443
You used a shovel before?

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.345
I have definitely
used a shovel.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.613
How far down we going?

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.347
Farther.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.915
Do you feel that heat?

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:56.916
And more.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:57.951
It's OK.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.152
We have the sun for 24 hours.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.220
So we have plenty of time.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.421
This is true.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.356
The heat in here is insane.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.791
How big a hole do you want?

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.559
Until we see a good bubble.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.494
[bleep] now, Siggi.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.895
Yeah, you hit the
spot right here.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.730
Right, you sound like my wife.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.998
[laughing]

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.733
Keep shoveling.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.634
More to the right.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.568
More To the right.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.569
OK, Siggi.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.005
You don't have to
get vicious on me.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.273
SIGGI: That's perfect.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.709
Put the pot now on
top of the bubbles.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.710
Exactly, yes.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.611
Really?

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.513
Yeah.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.914
OK.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.148
GORDON RAMSEY: Yes, it's hot.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.416
SIGGI: It looks pretty good.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:31.451
GORDON RAMSEY: And
bubbling away like mad.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.585
SIGGI: Yeah.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.553
GORDON RAMSEY: But the
temperature that's hot.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.654
It's really hot.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.356
SIGGI: Yeah, it's above
boiling temperature.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.624
GORDON RAMSEY: That water
when you get down, trust me,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.025
is piping hot.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.294
What a magical way of cooking.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:45.064
No gas, no electric,
just a beautiful spring.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.499
You're almost done.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.469
Now we put the
rock on top of it.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.572
We want to market, you know.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.640
Beautiful.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:54.841
Seriously?

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.810
Now, how long is that
going to take to cook?

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.112
24 hours.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.981
Siggi, I have not
got 24 hours, trust me.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.316
I already baked one.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.285
So why didn't we just
go straight to that one?

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.686
You made me dig that hole.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:10.790
Well, I mean, you don't
want to miss all the fun.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:11.724
This is it.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.792
This is it.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.161
OK, moment of truth.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.263
GORDON RAMSEY: - And
this one in 24 hours ago?

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.998
SIGGI: Yeah, can you hear it?

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.266
GORDON RAMSEY: I can hear it.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.367
That's incredible.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.569
Listen to that bubbling.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.470
SIGGI: Yeah, yeah.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.005
GORDON RAMSEY: That is insane.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.776
SIGGI: Put it over here.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:30.710
GORDON RAMSEY: Siggi.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.178
SIGGI: It's a beauty.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.547
GORDON RAMSEY: Honestly,
you're not just a pretty face.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.248
[laughing]

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.383
That looks beautiful.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.518
That smells delicious.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.352
Yeah, it does.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.120
Look at the color of it.

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.288
All from in there.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:45.625
Ready?

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.526
Yeah.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.394
[clanging]

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:50.897
GORDON RAMSEY: Oh.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:51.998
My God.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.066
Stop it.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.000
Stop.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.201
SIGGI: Perfect.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.203
That rye, I mean,
it smells amazing.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.539
I just-- Mmm.

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:01.174
May I just take a little slice?

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.308
Absolutely.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.077
GORDON RAMSEY: Oh, my Lord.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.445
Siggi, I'm in heaven.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:06.412
SIGGI: Yeah.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.283
Look at that.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.051
GORDON RAMSEY: Oh.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.453
Oh, my God.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.555
I just want to dive in there.

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.123
This is beautiful.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.658
SIGGI: And then--

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.526
GORDON RAMSEY: Oh.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.763
Something quite special
about slicing warm bread.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.764
And then on--

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.032
SIGGI: On top of the bread?

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:26.799
GORDON RAMSEY: Amazing.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.201
SIGGI: Exactly.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.103
GORDON RAMSEY: I mean,
this is the most glamorous

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.671
buffet in Iceland tonight.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:32.605
Cheers.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.006
Look at that.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.040
Cheers.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.675
Food fit for a Viking.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:36.576
Yeah.

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:37.510
Come on.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:40.413
Come on.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.749
Mmm, wow.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.083
Goes well together, you know.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.952
That is delicious.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:48.755
Honestly, a marriage
made in a volcano.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.456
It's rich, very dense.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.692
It's sweet and salty as
well at the same time.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:53.826
Yeah.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.695
It's got me thinking
because this technique

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.030
with rye bread amazing.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.031
Thank you.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.198
Chef to chef, thank you, bud.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:04:59.932
Very nice meeting you.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:00.566
Take care.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.968
You, too.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.136
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICE OVER): That
was an extraordinary rye bread.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.337
And Siggi was right.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:07.407
Unlike one I've ever tasted.

